We come home from the park.
I look at the clock.
It is exactly eight o'clock now.
Asha's rule is very strict.
Moti must be given food at exactly eight o'clock.
He is very hungry.
He jumps around me happily.
"Moti, wait!" I tell him firmly.
"You must not jump now," I say.
He sits down quietly and looks at me.
I take out his food in a metal bowl.
I place that bowl on the floor.
"Take this," I say to him.
"This is your food."
"Now eat it," I command.
He goes to the bowl immediately.
He eats his food quickly.
I smile and stroke his back.
